subject: fix(thinking): let a transport declare its thinking shape; nest reasoning on OpenCode Go /responses

A Responses-format client routed to an OpenCode Go model that also serves
/responses (deepseek-v4*, gpt-*-luna, grok-4.*) was passed through to
https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/responses without translation. applyThinking
then resolved the model's thinking format, which describes the Chat wire
(e.g. "deepseek" for deepseek-v4.1-flash), and wrote Chat-shaped fields
(thinking:{type}, reasoning_effort) into the Responses body. The upstream
answered 503 "Endpoint is unavailable", so any request asking for reasoning
effort failed and a combo silently fell through to the next model.

- A transports[] entry may now declare thinkingFormat; for that endpoint it
  wins over the model's thinkingFormat, which describes the Chat wire.
- opencode-go and muse declare thinkingFormat: "openai-responses" on their
  /responses entry, so the body carries reasoning:{effort,summary} instead.
- The hardcoded provider === "muse" branch in resolveFormat is removed; Muse
  output is unchanged.
- Chat routes are untouched, and providers without the declaration keep their
  current behaviour.

Refs #3014

